    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Umeclidinium 62.5 micrograms with vilanterol 25 micrograms, one inhalation each morning; albuterol as needed; no inhaled corticosteroid. [S]</item><item>Check inhaler technique and adherence at every visit. [S]</item><item>No long-term or ambulatory oxygen; reassess if resting saturation falls or he becomes more breathless. [S]</item><item>Pulmonary rehabilitation twice a week for about ten weeks, with six-minute walks at entry and exit. [S]</item><item>Low-dose CT for lung cancer screening now and yearly while eligible. [S]</item><item>COPD action plan, spoken and written; autumn vaccines. [S]</item><item>Spirometry in a year; report results with race-neutral equations. [S]</item><item>Pulmonology review if he has two moderate exacerbations or a hospital stay, or if his saturations fall. [S]</item><item>Discussed with Dr. Whitaker-Osei, who saw him the same day. The spirometry results, the reference equations and the plan were explained to Mr. Paige with his own numbers; he asked whether the old way of scoring would have changed his care, and was told that it could have made his disease look milder than it is. The inhaler technique was taught and he demonstrated it correctly. [S]</item><item>Follow-up: Dr. Whitaker-Osei continues his care at eight and fifteen weeks; pulmonology will see him again for repeated exacerbations, a hospital stay or falling oxygen levels. [S]</item></list></text>

